    {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "WHAT VA DISABILITY COMPENSATION IS"
    },
    {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
            {
                "text": "VA disability is a monthly, tax-free benefit paid by the U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs to veterans with a service-connected disability ("
            },
            {
                "text": "VA.gov — Eligibility",
                "url": "https://www.va.gov/disability/eligibility/"
            },
            {
                "text": "). Federal income tax does not apply ("
            },
            {
                "text": "IRS",
                "url": "https://www.irs.gov/individuals/military/special-tax-considerations-for-veterans"
            },
            {
                "text": "); most states also exempt it, but state treatment varies."
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
            {
                "text": "It is distinct from a few other programs you may have heard of:"
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "ordered": false,
        "items": [
            {
                "spans": [
                    {
                        "text": "VA pension",
                        "bold": true
                    },
                    {
                        "text": " is a separate, needs-based benefit for low-income wartime veterans ("
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "VA.gov — Pension",
                        "url": "https://www.va.gov/pension/eligibility/"
                    },
                    {
                        "text": ")."
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "spans": [
                    {
                        "text": "SSDI",
                        "bold": true
                    },
                    {
                        "text": " is paid by the Social Security Administration for a disability that prevents substantial work, regardless of cause ("
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "SSA.gov",
                        "url": "https://www.ssa.gov/benefits/disability/"
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "). Many veterans receive VA disability and SSDI at the same time."
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "spans": [
                    {
                        "text": "Military retirement",
                        "bold": true
                    },
                    {
                        "text": " is a separate DoD benefit for service members who meet the retirement criteria. Concurrent receipt rules (CRDP / CRSC) govern how retirement and VA disability interact for eligible retirees ("
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "DFAS — CRDP",
                        "url": "https://www.dfas.mil/RetiredMilitary/disability/crdp/"
                    },
                    {
                        "text": ")."
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "WHO MAY QUALIFY"
    },
    {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
            {
                "text": "To qualify for service connection, a veteran generally needs a current diagnosis, an in-service event or exposure, and a medical nexus linking the two ("
            },
            {
                "text": "VA.gov — Eligibility",
                "url": "https://www.va.gov/disability/eligibility/"
            },
            {
                "text": "). A condition can also be service-connected as a "
            },
            {
                "text": "secondary",
                "bold": true
            },
            {
                "text": " if it was caused or aggravated by another service-connected condition ("
            },
            {
                "text": "38 CFR §3.310",
                "url": "https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-38/chapter-I/part-3/subpart-A/section-3.310"
            },
            {
                "text": ")."
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
            {
                "text": "Eligibility is fact-specific. Whether your situation meets the legal standard depends on the evidence in your file. If you are unsure, an accredited VSO can review the facts with you at no charge ("
            },
            {
                "text": "VA accreditation search",
                "url": "https://www.va.gov/ogc/apps/accreditation/"
            },
            {
                "text": ")."
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
